{%- style -%}
  .fm-care-page {
    background-color: var(--fm-ivory);
    padding: clamp(50px, 8vw, 90px) 0;
  }
  .fm-care-header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto 56px auto;
  }
  .fm-care-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--fm-font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    color: var(--fm-forest);
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
  }
  .fm-care-card {
    background: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid var(--fm-border);
    padding: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .fm-care-card h2 {
    font-family: var(--fm-font-serif);
    font-size: 2.6rem;
    color: var(--fm-forest);
    margin: 0 0 20px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fm-border-light);
    padding-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .fm-care-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .fm-care-list-item {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    padding-left: 28px;
    position: relative;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #4F4D4A;
  }
  .fm-care-list-item::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 8px;
    color: var(--fm-gold);
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    top: 2px;
  }
  .fm-care-bold {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fm-forest);
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="fm-care-page">
  <div class="fm-container-narrow">
    <div class="fm-care-header">
      <span class="fm-value-tagline">MAINTENANCE & SIZING GUIDE</span>
      <h1>Rug Care & Selection Guide</h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.6rem; color: #55524E; line-height: 1.7;">Maximize your rug's life — everything you need to look after your handcrafted piece and choose the perfect proportion for your space.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: General Rug Care -->
    <div class="fm-care-card">
      <h2>General Rug Care & Maintenance Guidelines</h2>
      <ul class="fm-care-list">
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Sunlight Exposure:</span> Limit continuous and direct exposure to intense sunlight to prevent natural dye fading.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Rug Rotation:</span> Periodically rotate your rug 180 degrees every 6 months to ensure even wear across high-traffic pathways.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Dealing with Loose Threads:</span> If you notice loose threads or sprouting tufts, carefully trim them flush with scissors — never pull them.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Furniture Protectors:</span> Place felt protectors under heavy furniture legs to prevent pile crushing.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Shedding Period:</span> Expect natural minor shedding during the first few months. This is a standard characteristic of virgin wool and subsides with routine vacuuming.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Professional Cleaning:</span> Have your rug professionally cleaned every 2–3 years by trusted area rug specialists.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Spill Management:</span> Blot spills immediately using a clean, dry, white absorbent cloth. Avoid rubbing, which pushes pigments deeper into the fibers.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Ventilation:</span> Periodically turn the rug upside down outdoors and gently beat the back to release embedded micro-dust.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: Vacuuming Advice -->
    <div class="fm-care-card">
      <h2>Vacuuming Regularly</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 1.55rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #55524E; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Vacuum frequently using a low-power suction setting without a beater bar or rotating brush.
      </p>
      <ul class="fm-care-list">
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Gentle Suction:</span> Avoid high-powered rotating beater bars, which can pull delicate tufted loops.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Canister Vacuums:</span> Flat suction heads and smooth floor attachments are ideal.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Edges & Fringes:</span> Avoid vacuuming directly over serged edges or hand-tied fringes.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 3: Safe Storage -->
    <div class="fm-care-card">
      <h2>Tips for Storing Rugs Safely</h2>
      <ul class="fm-care-list">
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Proper Rolling:</span> Always roll the rug with the pile facing outwards. Never fold a hand-tufted rug.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Breathable Wrapping:</span> Wrap in breathable cotton fabric or acid-free paper rather than airtight plastic to prevent moisture trapping.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Elevated Storage:</span> Store horizontally in a cool, dry, ventilated area off the ground. Avoid placing heavy boxes on top.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 4: Sizing Guidelines -->
    <div class="fm-care-card">
      <h2>Sizing — How to Pick the Right Rug</h2>
      <ul class="fm-care-list">
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">1. Measure First:</span> Measure room boundaries and note door swings and furniture anchors.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">2. Opt for Larger Sizes:</span> A generous rug grounds furniture legs and expands visual perceived space.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">3. The 18-Inch Rule:</span> Maintain roughly 12–18 inches of exposed flooring between the rug edge and walls.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 5: Measuring Abstract & Amoebic Rugs -->
    <div class="fm-care-card">
      <h2>Measuring an Abstract-Shaped or Amoebic Rug</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 1.55rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #55524E; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Curvilinear, organic, and amoebic rugs create dynamic artistic focal points. To measure properly:
      </p>
      <ul class="fm-care-list">
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Outline with Painter's Tape:</span> Map the freeform curve on your floor with removable tape to visualize clearance around sofas and tables.</li>
        <li class="fm-care-list-item"><span class="fm-care-bold">Maximum Points of Axis:</span> Measure the widest length from extreme tip to extreme tip, and the widest perpendicular width.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

